  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "OcvcwTkwqtp+J3u+E+DloPGDgDc=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:36:03.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "`@powerhousedao/shared/processors/drive-analytics` (re-exported as `@powerhousedao/common/analytics` -- `packages/common/package.json` maps the `\"./analytics\"` subpath to `./drive-analytics.ts`, so the internal filename kept the old name but the public subpath did not) exports two processors plus a `processorFactory` that returns both per drive:\n\n- **`DriveAnalyticsProcessor`** \u2014 filters to `powerhouse/document-drive` and writes the `DriveOperations` metric, value always `1`, for `ADD_FILE`, `ADD_FOLDER`, `UPDATE_FILE`, `UPDATE_NODE`, `MOVE_NODE`, `COPY_NODE`, `DELETE_NODE`. It derives an `actionType` of `CREATED`/`DUPLICATED`/`UPDATED`/`MOVED`/`REMOVED` and a `target` of `NODE` or `DRIVE`.\n- **`DocumentAnalyticsProcessor`** \u2014 no `documentType` filter at all, so it counts the `DocumentOperations` metric across every document type, tagging `target` as `DRIVE` when the document *is* the drive.\n\nBoth are pure counters: `value: 1` per operation, dated by `operation.action.timestampUtcMs` / `operation.timestampUtcMs`, with the aggregation left entirely to query-time granularity and level of detail.\n\n**The \"enabled by default\" claim is stale.** The draft doc states that Connect enables drive analytics by default through a `ReactorAnalyticsProvider` component in `apps/connect/src/context/reactor-analytics.tsx`. At 6.2.2-dev.45 that component no longer exists, and `apps/connect/src/connect.config.ts` reads:\n\n```typescript\n// Analytics off by default; flip to true (or wire a runtime-config field)\n// when we want analytics enabled out of the box.\nisAnalyticsEnabled: false,\n```\n\nConnect's boot path registers processors only from installed packages that export a `processorFactory` \u2014 there is no built-in registration of the drive-analytics factory. A `driveAnalyticsEnabled` flag does survive, fed from `PH_CONNECT_DRIVE_ANALYTICS_ENABLED`, alongside `isAnalyticsExternalProcessorsEnabled`. So treat these two processors as a ready-made factory you opt into, not as ambient telemetry you already have.\n\nProvenance: draft `04-Reference/04-Processors/_07-DriveAnalyticsHooks.md` for the metric/dimension design; the enablement correction comes from `packages/shared/processors/drive-analytics/index.ts`, `apps/connect/src/connect.config.ts` and `apps/connect/src/store/reactor.ts` at 6.2.2-dev.45, which contradict the draft.\n\n_Source-verified 2026-08-13 against Powerhouse source at v6.2.2-dev.45._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T12:36:03.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:36:03.000Z"
    }
  },
